    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "10.2: Pass or Fail",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Your teacher will give you a bag with paper slips inside that are marked as either Pass or Fail. Do not empty the bag to look at all of the contents at once.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "10.2: Pass or Fail",
      "SourceExcerpt": "One partner should hold the bag so that the other partner cannot see inside while they draw a slip of paper. The other partner should draw 10 slips of paper from the bag, one at a time. After the 10 slips are drawn, record the number of…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "10.2: Pass or Fail",
      "SourceExcerpt": "From the results of the first trial, estimate the proportion of the slips in the bag that are marked Pass.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "10.2: Pass or Fail",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Switch roles with your partner and repeat the process until you have run 5 trials. For each trial, compute the proportion of slips you drew that are marked Pass.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "10.2: Pass or Fail",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Create a dot plot based on the trials from the class that shows the proportion of slips drawn that are marked Pass.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "10.2: Pass or Fail",
      "SourceExcerpt": "From the class dot plot, estimate the proportion of slips marked Pass in the bag. Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A biologist is breeding fruit flies to include a specific genetic mutation that will be useful in understanding memory in humans. To check whether a fly has the mutation, a DNA sequence is analyzed in a way that kills the fly, so the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Attribution: Gray and Black Fruit Fly, by pixabay. Public Domain. pexels. Source.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The biologist selects 40 flies to sequence at random and finds that 9 of them have the genetic mutation.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Based on this sample, estimate the proportion of flies in this group that has the genetic mutation.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Assume the sample is representative of the population of flies and create a simulation that mimics what the scientist found. Andre gets 200 pieces of paper and marks 45 of them as Mutant and puts them all in a bag. Since Andre decided to…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Andre then simulates the scientist’s sample by drawing a slip of paper from the bag noting whether it is Mutant or not, then replacing the paper into the bag and drawing another paper until he has a sample of 40. He repeats this process…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Andre then finds the mean proportion from his simulations to be 0.2195 and the standard deviation to be 0.06. How far are your values from the last question from the mean? This will represent your estimated margin of error.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Divide the distance from the last question by the standard deviation to get the margin of error in terms of the number of standard deviations.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The scientist is worried that only having one sample may not be reliable for estimating the proportion of flies with the mutation, but does not want to sacrifice more flies to get a larger sample. The proportion from the sample is a good…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Based on Andre’s simulations, should the scientist feel confident that the proportion of flies is within two standard deviations of the mean for the simulations?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Suppose the biologist breeds 600 flies. What is the minimum number of flies the biologist should expect to have the mutation based on Andre’s margin of error? What is the maximum that should be expected?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Although reality doesn’t always match up with our estimates, using sample data to estimate a characteristic for a larger group can be very useful, especially when you attach a margin of error to the estimate. It is unlikely that an…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, a lumber manufacturer may be worried about the number of boards it produces that are not straight. It would be too time consuming and costly to check every board, but they can check 50 boards each day to get an idea of the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The next day, their sample has 15 boards that are not straight out of the 50 checked. The manufacturer should estimate that the proportion of boards that are not straight for that day is about 0.3 (since \\(\\frac{15}{50} = 0.3\\) ) with a…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L10-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Fly Memory",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The maximum expected difference between an estimate for a population characteristic and the actual value of the population characteristic.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l10.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
